      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). Doses that high carry a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nTwo other points:\n- **Prescriber:** A licensed prescriber should place or confirm the order, since you've said you're not a clinician. If a clinician wants this order, they can tell me directly.\n- **Possible typo:** The intended dose may have been 1600 mg per day, or 400 mg or 800 mg per dose.\n\nHere are some orders I can enter once they're confirmed:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily\n\nTell me which dose the prescriber wants, or give me the corrected dose, and I'll enter it."
      }
