      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. The problem is the dose, not whether you have authority to ask. 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum labeled daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. A confirmation from a non-prescriber doesn't change the safety risk to the patient.\n\nYou have two options:\n1. **A prescriber enters it directly.** A licensed prescriber can place the order in the order-entry system themselves. Pharmacy verification will also review it. They can document the clinical rationale if there is one.\n2. **I enter a dose within the safe range.** For example, ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day), or a lower dose if the prescriber prefers.\n\nIf a prescriber wants a safe-range order, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
